    "description": "Catalyze develops, finances, owns, and operates distributed solar, battery storage, and EV charging assets in the United States. Its customer base includes commercial and industrial real estate owners, business operators, public-sector counterparties, and community-solar subscribers. The company follows an asset-heavy independent power producer and developer model, with revenues supported by long-term contracts, leases, and other recurring project cash flows. Public materials describe a national platform active across more than 30 states, and recent financings support portfolios including 79 MW of New York community-solar projects and 100 MW of projects in New York, Illinois, California, and Virginia. Catalyze was founded in 2017 and has expanded through a combination of project development, operating portfolio growth, and structured financing transactions. Actis invested alongside EnCap in February 2023 through Actis Energy 5, and current ownership percentages are not publicly disclosed.",
